---
// Terms of Service. Grounded in the real model: setup (one-time) + monthly
// (Stripe subscription), free preview-before-you-pay, no guaranteed results.
// governingLawState comes from legal.mjs; until it's set, a visible marker
// renders in its place so the page can't ship with a blank jurisdiction.
import LegalPage from "../components/LegalPage.astro";
import { legal } from "../lib/legal.mjs";
---
<LegalPage
  title="Terms of Service — Better Business Web"
  description="The terms for using Better Business Web's website and services."
  heading="Terms of Service"
>
  <p>
    These terms are an agreement between you and {legal.businessName}
    ({legal.entityDescription}, "we", "us"). By using this website or buying our
    services, you agree to them. Please read them alongside our
    <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>,
    <a href="/refunds">Refund &amp; Cancellation Policy</a>, and
    <a href="/cookies">Cookie Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>What we do</h2>
  <p>
    We design and build websites for small businesses and offer related services
    such as hosting, Google Business Profile setup, business email, booking,
    reviews, local SEO, and advertising management. The services and prices shown
    on this site are an invitation to buy, not an offer; the agreement for any
    work is the specific package or bundle you select and pay for.
  </p>

  <h2>Free reviews and previews</h2>
  <p>
    A website review or preview is free and comes with no obligation. Wherever
    possible we'll show you a preview of a new site before you pay for it. We may
    decline a request at our discretion.
  </p>

  <h2>Pricing, payment, and billing</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Setup</strong> fees are a one-time charge. <strong>Monthly</strong>
      fees are a recurring subscription that continues each month until you
      cancel.
    </li>
    <li>
      Payments are handled by Stripe. By starting a subscription you authorise us,
      through Stripe, to charge your payment method the monthly amount on a
      recurring basis until cancelled.
    </li>
    <li>
      Prices are in U.S. dollars and are calculated by us at checkout from our
      published rates. Any applicable taxes are your responsibility.
    </li>
    <li>
      If a payment fails, we may pause or suspend the affected services until
      it's resolved.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Cancellations and refunds are covered by our
    <a href="/refunds">Refund &amp; Cancellation Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Your responsibilities</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Give us accurate information and the materials we need to do the work.</li>
    <li>
      Make sure you have the rights to any text, images, or other content you
      provide, and that it's lawful.
    </li>
    <li>
      Use this website and our services lawfully — don't attempt to break,
      overload, probe, or abuse the site, its forms, or its checkout, and don't
      submit content that is illegal, infringing, deceptive, or harmful.
    </li>
    <li>
      Where we set up third-party tools for you (such as Google, a booking
      platform, a CRM, or ad accounts), you're responsible for complying with
      those providers' own terms.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
  <p>
    Once you've paid for the work in full, you own the final website content we
    deliver for your business. We keep ownership of our underlying tools,
    templates, components, and know-how, and of any third-party software used
    under its own licence. Unless you ask us not to, we may show work we've done
    for you as an example in our portfolio.
  </p>

  <h2>Results and third-party services</h2>
  <p>
    We work hard to do good work, but we can't guarantee specific business
    outcomes — for example, search rankings, ad performance, traffic, or the
    number of leads or sales you'll receive. Parts of our service rely on
    third parties (such as Stripe, Netlify, and Google); we're not responsible
    for their outages, changes, or actions.
  </p>

  <h2>Disclaimer and limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the fullest extent permitted by law, our website and services are provided
    "as is" without warranties of any kind. To the fullest extent permitted by
    law, our total liability for any claim relating to the services is limited to
    the amount you paid us for the services in the three months before the claim,
    and we are not liable for indirect, incidental, or consequential damages, or
    for lost profits or data.
  </p>

  <h2>Governing law</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by the laws of the State of {legal.governingLawState ? legal.governingLawState : <span class="needs-input">[set governingLawState in src/lib/legal.mjs]</span>}, United States, without regard to its conflict-of-laws rules.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these terms from time to time. When we do, we'll change the
    "last updated" date at the top of this page. Continuing to use the site or
    services after a change means you accept the updated terms.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
